Honesty: at confirm time pid **1524290** was

    bash …/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build …/oodac/main.oo …/oodac/oodac

That is **not** `ci_product.oo`. It is a live writer on the tree ELF.
Would also be a restore race. Did not copy over it. Did not start
another build.

bootstrap_no_cargo.oo (read only): `rm -f "$STAGE1"` with
STAGE1=`oodac/oodac` before `bootstrap/oodac_pure_build` rewrite. That is the
"ci may delete tree oodac" path. ci_product.oo itself has no `rm` of
that ELF; it calls bootstrap. Mid-bootstrap the tree ELF can vanish
even when a later writer is still live.

